<title>NEW ZEALAND: Colonial yr profit up 52.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Colonial yr profit up 52.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 13.00 vs 8.51</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 42.0 vs 27.5</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 15.0 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Turnover				  425.16 vs 402.56</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    17.77 vs 13.82</p>
<p>    Tax					   4.63 vs 5.17</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 30.95 vs same</p>
<p>Pay date Oct 7</p>
<p>Reg date Sept 27</p>
<p>    Ex div   Sept 30</p>
<p>Note - The Colonial Motor Corp Ltd, 33.9 percent-owned by Guinness Peat Group is a car dealership. Directors said they intended to honour their commitment and expect to pay a further 70 NZ cents per share by mid April 1997, subject to property sales. Following these payments, shareholders' equity would fall to NZ$73.4 million from $95.1 million.</p>
</text>
